course: dictionary
lesson: 348
title: Another: one more or a different one
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Another is a small word with a big job. It means one more of the same kind, or a different one. «Have another cookie» means one more cookie. «Try another way» means a different way.
explain: Look at the words after it to decide which meaning fits. In «Dev from another school beats Sam», another comes before school, so it means a different school. Ask yourself: is it one more of the same thing, or a different one?
explain: Another can also stand alone, as a pronoun. In «one dog barked at another», another means some other dog, so you do not need to repeat the word dog. Swap in a different one and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Another means one more of the same kind, or a different one.
fact: When «another» comes before a noun, it is a determiner: «another school», «another website», «another language».
fact: When «another» stands on its own, it is a pronoun and means some other person or thing.
fact: «One another» means each other, as in «they helped one another».
fact: «Another time» and «another day» mean a later time or a different day.
exercise: «Try another way up the hill.» What does another mean here? | The same way again | A way down the hill | No way at all | *A different way
exercise: «Dev from another school beats Sam in the final.» Is it the same school or a different one? | A school that is closed | A school just for dogs | The same school | *A different school
exercise: In «one dog barked at another», which word stands in for a second dog? | *another | barked | dog | one
test: «Real game companies never ask for your password on another website.» What does another website mean? | *A different website | A website you have already visited | A website that asks for money | A website for games only
test: In «Have another cookie», is another a determiner or a pronoun? | Verb, because it shows an action | *Determiner, because it goes before a noun | Pronoun, because it stands alone | Noun, because it names a thing
exam: In «If someone tells you a hurtful thing another person said, check with that person directly», what does another person mean? | A kind person | *A different person | A teacher | The same person again
